        Color resources for the application theme.

        FIXED:
        1. All colors referenced in themes.xml (purple_500, purple_700, teal_200, teal_700, white, black) are now defined.
        2. This resolves the Android resource linking failure: "resource color/purple_500 not found" and similar errors in values.xml and values-night-v8.xml.
        3. Values match the default Material Design palette used in modern Android 14+ projects (2026 standards).
        4. No external sources used; based solely on standard Android color naming from the project manifest and theme parent.
    -->

    <color name="purple_200">#FFBB86FC</color>
    <color name="purple_500">#FF6200EE</color>
    <color name="purple_700">#FF3700B3</color>
    <color name="teal_200">#FF03DAC5</color>
    <color name="teal_700">#FF018786</color>
    <color name="black">#FF000000</color>
    <color name="white">#FFFFFFFF</color>
</resources>